.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Q1-SCALES** — ACCEPT the proposed normalisations (margin / 20 dB, SE / 4 bit/s/Hz, occupancy / 10 users, angle / 1 rad, times / 120 s, phase / 3); they are scales, not thresholds; sealed with the Q1 schema SHA in spec v1.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Q2-MISSING-PLACEMENT** — ACCEPT (after the nine current fields, before the offsets). **Q2-SCHEMA-SEAL** — the 22-field schema gets its own SHA in spec v1; the 21-field SHA 54ab6a82… is retired and never stamped again. **Q2-INCUMBENT-MARGIN** — each candidate row carries its **own candidate-current margin**; the incumbent's margin is a per-user context field broadcast once per row (both present, distinct names).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **C3-SET-REPRESENTATION** — set head input = permutation-invariant pooling (sum and max) over the changed users' per-user vectors (their Q1 row for the selected action, their incumbent row, `missing_incumbent`), concatenated with global resource context per affected beam (occupancy before/after, activation change, interference summary, cap margin), padded to |A| ≤ 4 with masks; a two-layer MLP on the pooled vector; anchored zeros by construction (output × 𝟙[|A| ≥ 2]). Shapley for reporting: exact over subsets for |A| ≤ 4.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **LEARNER-SEED-VALUES** — twelve learner seeds derived from domains `V025_LEARNER/seed/{1..12}` by the repository seed rule (no hand-picked integers); the external BASELINE's implementation sha256 is recorded in the allocation manifest.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:12:8. **DEADLINE-CLOCK** — wall clock (monotonic) on `sat`; coordinator worker count = 4 processes; no warm caches for decision timing (cold per anchor); the timing evidence is the per-phase table of stage 4c.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:13:9. **FORMAL-ALLOCATION** — at seal, by the assembler (worlds, dates, starts, seeds, 30-anchor coverage, stride, manifest digest).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:14:10. **EVENT-QOS** — Φ₁ = 0.5 κ for a same-satellite beam change, Φ₂ = 1.0 κ for a satellite change; re-entry after outage is priced as a satellite change if the satellite differs from the pre-outage incumbent, else as a beam change; a cell re-key at a dwell boundary without a beam change is not a handover (priced 0, counted separately). Interruption blackouts per stage-1 decision 5.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:15:11. **ZERO-BIT-DISPOSITION** — contract v1 §D3. **ZERO-QOS-BASELINE** — if the DROP arm's event count is zero and FULL's is positive, the relative handover/Φ margin fails by rule (`FAIL_UNDEFINED_DENOMINATOR`); if both are zero, non-inferior by rule; recorded per contrast.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.3-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 priority declaration — v1.3 erratum (controller, sealed before any successor outcome; 2026-09-08, server clock ≈ 16:30 UTC)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.3-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:6:v1.2 §1 says "Total: 28 primary-eligible cells + diagnostic U cells". The explicit list in the same paragraph governs and yields **25 primary-eligible settings** (5 architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` + S, H, SH, T for each of the five = 5 + 4 × 5) plus **6 diagnostic U settings** (`U-cap`, `U-margin` for `a-γ, b, a′-γ`; v1.2 §2), i.e. **31 settings in total**. The number 28 was a counting error; the explicit enumeration, its sealed priority order and the matrix digests of engine stage 2 (31 settings) are the authority. Flagged by the stage-2 engine report before any setting was evaluated on a real world.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 — controller decisions on compute budget and thinning order (2026-09-08 ≈ 17:50 UTC; before any real-world successor outcome)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:3:Source: provider v1 report — with the Python-object tape, the 57 525-chain cross-product inventory and the unbatched runner, the measured cost is 12.63 s per anchor of provider acquisition, 4.66 s per 48-boundary catalogue row, q ≈ 0.308, ≈ 182 868 core-hours for the plan (budget: 160). This is an engineering failure of the current implementation, not a property of the physics; the decisions below fix the implementation first and only then thin the plan, in a pre-declared order.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Engineering targets (stage 4, before any thinning):** dense per-step numpy tapes (provider decision 9); realisable inventory only (≈ 2 760 chains, decision 4/D4); batched evaluation of a whole catalogue per anchor — the capped fixed point, ACM lookup, energy and bits computed for all configurations of an anchor in one vectorised pass over (configuration × boundary); provider acquisition amortised once per world (48 × 30 boundaries computed once and shared by all settings and arms). Target: ≤ 0.02 s per catalogue row per anchor and ≤ 1 s per anchor of provider work on the reference hardware; the rehearsal reports both.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Catalogue size cap (decision 4 refined):** pairwise joint moves are restricted to the top-K = 10 users by nominal unilateral surplus **and their top-2 legal options each** (≤ 45 × 4 = 180 rows); unilateral rows ≤ users × legal options (≈ 2 700); evacuation sets ≤ active beams (≈ 40); S0 proposals ≤ 200. Catalogue ≤ ≈ 3 200 rows per anchor.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Thinning order if the rehearsed projection still exceeds 160 core-hours** (apply the smallest step that fits; record every applied step in the seal; never chosen by outcome): (i) anchor stride k = 2, then 3 (decision item 3); (ii) treatment settings dropped from the **bottom of the sealed priority order** (T cells first, then SH, then H, then S — within each, the lowest-priority architectures first); the five architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` and the U diagnostics are never dropped; (iii) probe worlds reduced from 4 to 3 only if (i)–(ii) are insufficient, and then the claim is labelled accordingly.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **What is never thinned:** the 12 + 1 arms per setting (the arms are the science), the 48-boundary integration, the calibration procedure, the placebo and dry-run.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **Reporting:** the rehearsal writes a cost table (per world: provider seconds; per anchor: rows, seconds; projection per setting) into the seal package; the projection and the applied thinning steps are sealed before the first unit opens.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 priority declaration — v1.2 amendment (controller, sealed before any successor outcome; 2026-09-08, server clock ≈ 15:50 UTC)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:3:v1.0 (sha e45f2f02…) and v1.1 (sha 6851d04b…) are preserved unchanged. This amendment applies the round-5 outside opinions (`OUTSIDE-ROUND5-CHATGPT-QA-2026-09-08.md`, `OUTSIDE-ROUND5-CHATGPT-DEEP-RESEARCH-2026-09-08.md`). No successor outcome exists at sealing time; the primary architecture and the priority order of v1.1 are unchanged.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:1. **Own sensitivity cells for the primary.** The rate-target primary (a-r) and its FDM sibling (a′-r) receive their own treatment cells so that robustness is not borrowed from a-γ: add `a-rS`, `a-rH`, `a-rSH`, `a-rT` and `a′-rS`, `a′-rH`, `a′-rSH`, `a′-rT` (treatments as defined in astra round 3 §4). Priority order becomes: `a-r0 > a′-r0 > a-γ0 > b0 > a′-γ0`, then S in the order `a-r, a′-r, a-γ, b, a′-γ`, then H, then SH, then T in the same architecture order; U cells remain diagnostic-only. Total: 28 primary-eligible cells + diagnostic U cells.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:7:2. **U split.** The uncapped-Shannon diagnostic is split into `U-cap` (SE cap removed, margin kept) and `U-margin` (cap kept, margin removed) for each of the three original architectures (6 diagnostic cells) so the two effects are separable. Diagnostic only; never primary-eligible.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:8:3. **Uncertainty reporting.** The primary uncertainty statement for every contrast is a **cluster bootstrap that recomputes ΣB/ΣE per resample** (clusters = TLE dates × training seeds as declared in the evaluation design); paired per-world log-EE intervals are supplementary and are never substituted for the pooled-ratio interval.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Claim wording.** The success claim is conditional and intersection–union: "with the other two components enabled, each of the three FULL − DROP pooled-EE contrasts exceeds its prespecified margin δ = +0.5 pp with the 95 % lower bound above it, and FULL is QoS non-inferior to each DROP"; the all-neutral cell supports the FULL − ALL_NEUTRAL comparison; main effects across all backgrounds are not claimed without the full 2³ factorial.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:10:5. **Φ semantics.** Because interruption (treatment H) already removes useful time, Φ₁/Φ₂ are declared to price *signalling/QoS preference* (not time, not joules); they are reported alongside the handover rate as co-primary QoS outcomes, and the reward/coordinator use the same event ledger and coefficients.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:11:6. **Treatment T** is the left-endpoint legacy snapshot (controller decision item 3) and is reported against the converged integral at the same decision instant.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:12:7. **Provenance labels** (from the Deep Research): γ*, r*, P_b/cap, W/α, SE_max, margin, SINR_min, OBO/p_sat, η_max/PA curve, standby (primary and sensitivity), circuit/baseband, bus exclusion, handover event energy, blackout mapping, Δt/quadrature, D2-derived gates and N = 4 refresh are all carried as **declared benchmark constants** (`VERIFY_SOURCE` where a physical claim would be implied); the paper's system-model section states this once. N = 4 is named a candidate-refresh period, not a dwell.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 priority declaration — v1.1 amendment (controller, sealed before any successor outcome; 2026-09-08, server clock ≈ 14:35 UTC)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:3:v1.0 (`V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md`, sha256 e45f2f025a230a7d66ddd16c3b369c52979c177f58927e016228e4b3dc800020) is preserved unchanged. This amendment applies astra round 4 (`astra-physics-round4-final.md`: `PRIMARY=a-r | ADD_CELLS=a-r0,a′-r0 | R_STAR=50 Mbit/s (synthetic) | C1_LEVER_UNDER_RATE_TARGET=collapses`) and the fresh-context C3 adjudication's finding that a constant-SINR target does not create the occupancy → required-power mechanism. No successor outcome exists at sealing time.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:1. **Primary architecture: (a-r) `V025-ANGLE-RATE-TPC-TDM-ACM`** — memoryless angle-aware power control with a per-user nominal rate target r* = 50 000 000 bit/s (inherited as a synthetic operating point from Track B lever L1; explicitly not calibrated demand). Equal-airtime full-band TDM. Required SINR from the frozen ACM profile: Γ_r(n_b) = min{γ_m : W·SE_m/n_b ≥ r*}; slot power p_u = min(1.65 W, Γ_r(n_b)·(N₀W + Î_u)/ĥ_u), ĥ_u = G^T(θ_u)·L_u·G^R; history-independent coupled solving; slot-integrated PA accounting. Angle drives power through ĥ_u; occupancy drives power through Γ_r(n_b).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Components under the primary:** C1 = whole-network difference surplus (its positive marginal is expected through energy and service, not surplus bits — accepted); C2 = future required-power / cap / service-survival forecasts (astra round 3 §2 items 26–28); C3 = set-level coordinator scoring whole configurations, with coordinated load transfers / swaps included alongside evacuations, one prospectively frozen catalogue across matched arms.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:10:5. **Admission (unchanged):** acceptance suite, QoS, genuine joint-headroom witness, S0 deployable gain ≥ 1 %, FULL/DROP marginals; goal 2 requires all three positive; the primary's identity cannot change with outcome signs.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:11:6. **First probe cell:** a-r0 on fresh shared TRAIN tapes with FULL, all DROP arms, unilateral / joint / deployable S0 arms and NULL / random-feasible controls. Stage A remains HOLD until admission.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 physics successor — priority declaration (controller, sealed before any successor outcome; 2026-09-08, server clock ≈ 13:50 UTC)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:9:- **Primary system model: architecture (a) `V025-ANGLE-TPC-TDM-ACM`** — memoryless angle-aware power control (per 30.08 s step, per simultaneous slot configuration: p_u = min(1.65 W, γ*·(N + Î_u)/ĥ_u), ĥ_u = G^T(θ_u)·L_u·G^R, γ* = the 8PSK 2/3 threshold of EN 302 307-1 Table 13 with the 1.7 dB margin and roll-off 0.20 correction, i.e. 7.528 dB nominal; equal-airtime TDM; coupled nominal powers solved from a history-independent initialisation with frozen tolerance and residual certification; no segment memory). Chosen because it is the only candidate that satisfies requirement 1 by construction. This choice is made **before** any successor outcome and is independent of C3's result.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:12:- **Priority order of the 18-cell physics-settings matrix (fixed now):** `a0 > b0 > a′0 > aS > bS > a′S > aH > bH > a′H > aSH > bSH > a′SH > aT > bT > a′T`; U cells (uncapped Shannon) are diagnostic only and ineligible as primary. Treatments per astra round 3 §4 (0 = 47-subinterval integration, standby 0, interruption off, ACM cap + margin; T = snapshot; S = standby f = 1/12; H = conditional 62/142 ms useful-time interruption; SH = both; U = uncapped).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:13:- **Everything else** follows astra round 3 §2 (items 1, 3, 5–31 unchanged: ACM table, margin, served ⇔ SINR ≥ −1.4418 dB after joint resolution, energy accounting with P_idle = 0 primary, clock/integration, geometry/10° visibility, actions, observable information, calibration λ = η_ref and κ on a nominal-greedy reference, reward core R = B − η_ref·E, Φ as QoS, C1 full-network difference surplus, C2 feature migration and forecast schema, C3 as set-level consolidation coordinator, learning contract, history seal) and §3 (known-answer suite, extended for (a) with coupled-power convergence/saturation and slot-consistent interference fixtures).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:17:- The primary is (a) by requirement 1, not by C3's outcome. C3's marginal is measured under every cell and reported as a regime map ("where does coordination change EE"). A positive C3 under (b) with a non-positive C3 under (a) is a reported finding, not grounds to swap the primary after the fact.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:18:- Training admission (astra §4): retained factors need positive oracle marginals beyond certified numerical error and acceptable QoS; C3 additionally needs genuine joint headroom (a multi-user witness beating the unilateral alternative) and a deployable S0 gain ≥ the pre-existing 1 % practical threshold. If C3's set-level oracle marginal is ≤ 0 in every completed, physically defensible cell, C3 training/screens/confirmation close and a bounded negative is reported; C1/C2 proceed under their own gates.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:19:- No target, standby, margin, service or priority change after outcomes are opened. Any defect found later is repaired and re-run, never demoted by outcome.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:24:3. Stage A regenerated sources + training (FULL2, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, ALL_NEUTRAL; three initialisations) only for factors admitted by the probes; stage C ladder; C3-S screens and confirmatory on fresh worlds.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 priority declaration — v1.5 amendment (controller, sealed before any formal successor outcome; 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:25 UTC)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:3:v1.0–v1.4 are preserved unchanged. This amendment applies the fresh-context first-principles review (`FIRST-PRINCIPLES-REVIEW-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-2026-09-08.md`: `MINIMAL_DESIGN_MATCHES_PLAN=PARTIAL | SMALLEST_MATRIX=1 setting | HIGHEST_RESIDUAL_RISK=learner/information 0.90`) and pipeline audit A. No priority, constant, arm or margin changes; the order of execution and the uncertainty estimator do.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Execution order and scope of the admission decision.** The training-admission decision (PHYSICS-GO) is made on the primary setting `a-r0` alone, as sealed in v1.1. The other 30 settings are **exploratory sensitivities**: they execute after `a-r0` completes, in the sealed priority order, within the remaining budget, and none of them can change the admission decision or the claim. The owner's requirement that the off-axis angle influence power and EE is demonstrated by the physics itself (a sealed KAT and figure of required power and EE versus off-axis angle under `a-r0`), not by matrix cells.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Executable set-score decomposition (from the review's pass 1(d)).** For a configuration with changed-user set A relative to the anchor reference a⁰ and F = B − η_ref·E: unilateral increments dᵢ = F(aᵢ, a⁰₋ᵢ) − F(a⁰); interaction residual Ψ_A = F(a_A, a⁰₋A) − F(a⁰) − Σᵢ∈A dᵢ. C1(config) = Σᵢ∈A dᵢ (+ Φ), C3(config) = Ψ_A (credited to users by the Shapley allocation of the interaction game; pairs = Ψ/2 each), C2(config) = the declared continuation value excluding the immediate term. Identity: C1 + C3 = F(a_A) − F(a⁰) exactly (KAT). Factor arms: FULL = C1 + C2 + C3; DROP_C1 = C2 + C3; DROP_C2 = C1 + C3; DROP_C3 = C1 + C2 (additive), all in the same selector class and catalogue (stage-4 item 18).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Primary uncertainty estimator.** Because dates and learner seeds are crossed (audit A), the primary interval for every contrast is a **two-way pigeonhole bootstrap** over TLE dates × learner seeds with arms paired within each resample and ΣB/ΣE recomputed per draw; the one-way cluster bootstrap of v1.2 §3 and the delta-method interval become supplementary. For the learner-free physics matrix the primary is the one-way bootstrap over TLE dates.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Claim-panel dates.** The successor's confirmation panel uses TRAIN dates that were never used by any successor development activity (probe, calibration, rehearsal, KAT, synthetic-real); the allocation manifest asserts this role-wise disjointness; overlap with legacy (old-physics) development dates is recorded, not forbidden, and the claim wording says so.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **TLE selection convention.** The legacy nearest-epoch rule (per NORAD, files date−1/date/date+1, |age| ≤ 24 h at episode start, future epochs allowed) is retained as an accuracy-first benchmark convention shared by all arms (`VERIFY_SOURCE`); it is documented as non-causal.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Information contract for C3 (residual risk 0.90).** Before any successor training, the stages 6–8 contract v1 must state exactly what the learned heads observe and what the coordinator computes (candidate identities, load, shared capacity and interference, activation state, other users' proposed actions or a joint search), with the deployment-capability manifest; retrained ablations are the scientific claim, checkpoint knockouts are reported separately.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.4-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 priority declaration — v1.4 erratum (controller, sealed before any formal successor outcome; 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:15 UTC)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.4-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **δ units.** The success margin is a **relative** pooled-EE gain: EE_FULL / EE_DROP − 1 ≥ +0.5 % (the phrase "+0.5 pp" in v1.2 §4 meant this relative percentage; pooled EE has no percentage-point scale). The 95 % lower bound of that relative gain must exceed +0.5 %.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.4-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Interval convention.** All bootstrap intervals are central 95 % percentile intervals (2.5th/97.5th percentiles, linear interpolation as implemented by `numpy.quantile` default); the one-sided decision uses the corresponding endpoint (2.5th for gains and availability, 97.5th for handover rate and Φ-priced cost), which is conservative relative to a 5 % one-sided bound and is retained as declared.

